{"author":{"id":"8d2e0405f08ac6c481f912544d6d5c0f58b2dc14a7e51ad4d499ee7a34567943"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794324855,"nonce":"Bk2gG0NI3VdhAkZ7L1/AeRJqf20=","title":"Does the transient default newton(reuse=True) pay when the factorization is not kept?","message":"fem.solve's transient default Newton keeps its tangent while it contracts. With a CPU lu() the factorization is redone on every solve anyway, so the kept tangent saves the assembly only and may cost extra Newton iterations. On a stiff reaction-diffusion march in jno.fdm (bdf2, lu()), the kept tangent was slower than a fresh newton(direct=True). Open: measure fem.solve marches (a stiff reaction, a stabilised flow) with reuse=True against a fresh tangent, per lu backend (superlu, pardiso, cudss), and pick the default per case.","files":null}]}